					) hide
					   (hide yes)
   )
			)
			(property "ki_description" "NEW C1 PRIMARY (state.json P3 decision, 2026-08-09, supersedes BFC280811339): Johanson 5602 air-dielectric trimmer, 1-30pF 250VDC(500VDC test) -65/+125C, Q>800@100MHz, top screwdriver-slot adjust, panel/PCB-mount threaded case + separate lead. Chosen over BFC280811339 because -65/+125C clears this board's 74-88C flange-adjacent operating range under 150W CW where the retired PP-film part's -40/+70C category temperature does not. NET ASSIGNMENT IS PHYSICAL (state.json P3 decision, 2026-08-09), not a rotor/stator inference: Pin 1=STATOR (case/thread/hex-collar assembly) -> GND. Pin 2=ROTOR (separate insulated lead wire) -> RF. A panel-mount trimmer's case is engineered to pass through a grounded metal panel, so the case is the ground-compatible terminal by construction, and it is also the only terminal a hand or tool actually brushes during tuning - so it must be grounded whatever its internal (rotor/stator) role is. See parts/5602.json and the footprint's own descr for the full reasoning."
				(id 9)
				(at 0 -25.4 0)
				(effects
					(font
						(size 1.27 1.27)
					) hide
					   (hide yes)
   )
			)
